{"name":"Mouldy Ochre","hex":"#d5a300","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mouldy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with mould.","Showing signs of neglect; disused."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A torpedo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mouldy"},{"term":"ochre","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clay earth pigment containing silica, aluminum and ferric oxide.","A somewhat dark yellowish orange colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a yellow-orange colour.","Referring to cultures that covered their dead with ochre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ochre"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mold","blocks":[{"text":"A mold or mould is one of the structures that certain fungi can form. The dust-like, colored appearance of molds is due to the formation of spores containing fungal secondary metabolites. The spores are the dispersal units of the fungi. Not all fungi form molds. Some fungi form mushrooms or ascomata; others grow as single cells and are called yeasts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Mold_on_a_strawberry.jpg/330px-Mold_on_a_strawberry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mold","wikidata":"Q159341"},{"title":"Ochre","blocks":[{"text":"Ochre is a family of natural clay earth pigments, made up of ferric oxide and varying amounts of clay and sand, ranging in colour from yellow to deep orange or brown. The term is also used for the colours produced by this pigment, especially a light brownish-yellow. A variant of ochre containing a large amount of hematite, or dehydrated iron oxide, has a reddish tint known as red ochre. The term \"ochre\" is colloquially used to cover a range of different substances used for their colours in Aboriginal Australian art and ceremonial decoration, for instance the clay known as \"white ochre\" or \"pipe clay\" is derived from kaolin or gypsum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Hellocker-_Pigment.JPG/330px-Hellocker-_Pigment.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ochre","wikidata":"Q12353401"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Mouldy_Clementine.jpg/500px-Mouldy_Clementine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Mouldy_Clementine.jpg/1280px-Mouldy_Clementine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Mouldy_Clementine.jpg/500px-Mouldy_Clementine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Penicillium digitatum mold growing on a clementine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMouldy_Clementine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Spinellus_fusiger_51504.jpg/500px-Spinellus_fusiger_51504.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Spinellus_fusiger_51504.jpg/500px-Spinellus_fusiger_51504.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spinellus fusiger growing on the mushroom Mycena haematopus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpinellus_fusiger_51504.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Ojmold1000xa.jpg/500px-Ojmold1000xa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Ojmold1000xa.jpg/500px-Ojmold1000xa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spores from green mold (Penicillium or Trichoderma) growing on an orange, 1000× wet mount","link":"https://en.wikip